message: "If you use these results, cite them via this metadata."
title: "Hadamard-B: bordered Goethals-Seidel arrays - characterisation, classification, and three equivalence classes at order 668"
abstract: >-
  An exact (iff) characterisation of extending a Goethals-Seidel array
  over a finite abelian group to a Hadamard matrix through a coset
  border of width 4s; within the house-Gram branch and under w > 2s,
  the classification of the surviving parameters (with n >= 3 the
  cells are (0,1), (1,1), and i = s+1 with s odd); the complete
  resolution of the s = 1 border system; machine verification of
  twelve publicly posted matrices through the theorems' hypotheses;
  and a proof that order 668 carries at least three Hadamard
  equivalence classes, pairwise separated by the exact 4-profile
  invariant. Provenance:
  the twelve parameter records are decoded from publicly posted
  matrices and carry no priority claim. AI-generated results with a
  human managing the workflow - produced by Claude Code (Fable 5,
  Anthropic); see DISCLOSURE.md. The authors field below records the
  repository owner and responsible publisher; the AI/human division of
  labour is DISCLOSURE.md. The two licenses are assigned by category,
  not jointly: code is MIT; the note and prose are CC BY-SA 4.0; the
  banked mathematical data carries no license claim - see
  LICENSE-DOCS.md.
type: software
